    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Max is standing in the kitchen, looking very confused as he discusses finances. Let's listen closely to their exchange in Russian first, and then walk through each line together.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Наша квартплата?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "В смысле?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "В прямом смысле.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Сейчас я тебе все объясню.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я ничего не понимаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Предположим одну ситуацию.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Тимур привозит нам коньяк.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Пять литров коньяка каждую неделю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Он привозит его бесплатно?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Да, абсолютно бесплатно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И что мы делаем с ним?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Этот коньяк идет на оплату.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let us break down this interaction.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Наша квартплата?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Our rent?' Max starts with 'rent' and pairs it with 'rent' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "В смысле?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What do you mean?' Max puts 'sense' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'sense'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "В прямом смысле.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Exactly what I said.' Here 'straight' sets up the idea, while 'sense' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Сейчас я тебе все объясню.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will explain everything to you now.' You'll hear 'now' all the time in the show, here connected with 'I'll explain'. Then Max replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я ничего не понимаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I do not understand anything.' The key word here means 'I', which Max combines with 'nothing'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Предположим одну ситуацию.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Let's assume one situation.' Ilya starts with 'suppose' and pairs it with 'one' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Тимур привозит нам коньяк.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Timur brings us cognac.' Ilya puts 'Timur' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'bring'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Пять литров коньяка каждую неделю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Five liters of cognac every week.' In Russian, 'five' leads into 'for a week' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Он привозит его бесплатно?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Does he bring it for free?' You'll hear 'he' all the time in the show, here connected with 'for free'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Да, абсолютно бесплатно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, absolutely for free.' A compact expression built around 'completely' and 'for free'. Max answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И что мы делаем с ним?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And what do we do with it?' Listen for the word meaning 'what' right alongside 'we' in this line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Этот коньяк идет на оплату.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This cognac goes to payment.' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'cognac' straight to 'payment'. Now let us listen to the conversation again without interruption.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
